WEBVTT

1
00:59:47.426 --> 00:59:50.306
Was it nice or not, to just hear each other's prayers?

2
00:59:50.306 --> 00:59:51.106
It was nice, right?

3
00:59:52.106 --> 00:59:52.906
Praise God.

4
00:59:54.706 --> 00:59:59.306
I specifically chose seven people, because seven is the number of fullness.

5
00:59:59.906 --> 01:00:01.706
And we stand here at the end of this year.

6
01:00:02.306 --> 01:00:05.106
I am really happy with what God has done in the past year.

7
01:00:05.306 --> 01:00:08.106
Hallelujah, I am really looking forward to 2025.

8
01:00:08.706 --> 01:00:13.306
I want to thank everyone in our church.

9
01:00:13.706 --> 01:00:18.306
I will now move on to the encouragement towards the collections.

10
01:00:18.706 --> 01:00:21.106
And you all know how it works in Open Church.

11
01:00:21.106 --> 01:00:25.506
We have QR codes and we have ways to give on our app.

12
01:00:26.106 --> 01:00:35.306
And I would prefer that everyone actually just in their monthly online banking...

13
01:00:35.506 --> 01:00:39.106
...makes a thoughtful and prayerful agreement with God.

14
01:00:39.106 --> 01:00:40.906
Lord, I want to give this part to you.

15
01:00:41.306 --> 01:00:44.506
And I say this very boldly, I say this very audaciously.

16
01:00:44.706 --> 01:00:45.906
That is what I would prefer.

17
01:00:46.306 --> 01:00:48.506
But I do not say this for my own wallet.

18
01:00:48.506 --> 01:00:51.706
But I say this because we as a church want to build further.

19
01:00:52.106 --> 01:00:53.506
And we want to be able to work further.

20
01:00:53.706 --> 01:00:57.306
But on the one hand, giving is something you give to God.

21
01:00:57.506 --> 01:01:02.706
On the other hand, giving is about being able to build together, to be able to save together.

22
01:01:03.506 --> 01:01:09.106
But what I always look at when I give, and I want to give this as advice to all of us.

23
01:01:09.506 --> 01:01:18.306
When I give, I often or usually my main reason for giving is always built on gratitude.

24
01:01:18.706 --> 01:01:22.306
For I understand where my income comes from.

25
01:01:22.306 --> 01:01:26.506
I understand where everything comes from that I have received from the Father.

26
01:01:26.506 --> 01:01:29.706
The Bible says everything that is good comes from the Father.

27
01:01:29.906 --> 01:01:35.106
And for me, when I came to repentance in the name of Jesus, it was for me that I said...

28
01:01:35.106 --> 01:01:41.506
...yes but Lord, I want to give something back to you like Abel that makes you happy.

29
01:01:41.506 --> 01:01:47.506
And then I also want to pray that God says I accept what Tim has given me.

30
01:01:47.506 --> 01:01:54.306
So I do not want to hold back for myself, but I want to give out of that gratitude to God.

31
01:01:54.306 --> 01:01:56.506
And yes, that can sometimes be a sacrifice.

32
01:01:56.906 --> 01:02:03.506
That can sometimes be a sacrifice that feels in your wallet, but yes feels in your gratitude.

33
01:02:03.906 --> 01:02:09.906
And that is why I have decided with my family that we will consistently give to the Lord.

34
01:02:09.906 --> 01:02:12.906
And that we simply say this part is for the Lord.

35
01:02:12.906 --> 01:02:17.306
And I want to encourage you for 2025, put your shoulders under it.

36
01:02:17.706 --> 01:02:19.306
Join Open Church.

37
01:02:19.306 --> 01:02:21.106
Be part of the church.

38
01:02:21.106 --> 01:02:24.306
And I say it a little bit, I exaggerate a little.

39
01:02:24.306 --> 01:02:32.906
But do not just come to church for too long in the form of I come, I take, and I go home again.

40
01:02:33.106 --> 01:02:34.506
But I do not participate further.

41
01:02:34.506 --> 01:02:37.506
I won't help further or contribute.

42
01:02:37.506 --> 01:02:43.506
You know, you are welcome and I don't work in the administration department.

43
01:02:43.506 --> 01:02:46.306
I don't know who gives, I don't know what someone gives.

44
01:02:46.306 --> 01:02:48.506
That's not what I want, I want to keep my distance from that.

45
01:02:48.506 --> 01:02:49.706
There are clear agreements about it.

46
01:02:49.706 --> 01:02:52.106
I don't want to know what is given.

47
01:02:52.106 --> 01:02:55.506
And that's why I can freely say, participate.

48
01:02:55.506 --> 01:02:58.506
Participate so we can build together.

49
01:02:58.506 --> 01:03:01.306
We are saving for a new construction project together.

50
01:03:01.306 --> 01:03:03.106
And I just want to ask everyone.

51
01:03:03.106 --> 01:03:05.906
Don't let it depend on a few people.

52
01:03:05.906 --> 01:03:09.306
But let's all participate together in the name of Jesus.

53
01:03:09.306 --> 01:03:11.106
Is that an agreement?

54
01:03:11.106 --> 01:03:14.106
That's a good agreement, hallelujah.

55
01:03:14.106 --> 01:03:16.306
Praise God.

56
01:03:16.306 --> 01:03:19.706
I want to invite Vanessa, my dear wife, to the stage.

57
01:03:19.706 --> 01:03:21.306
Because we are moving on to the Word.

58
01:03:21.306 --> 01:03:24.106
Did you bring your Bible?

59
01:03:24.106 --> 01:03:26.106
Hallelujah.

60
01:03:27.106 --> 01:03:31.106
Thank you, beloved.

61
01:03:31.106 --> 01:03:36.106
Can we thank the providers?

62
01:03:36.106 --> 01:03:43.106
Can I be a bit more vocal?

63
01:03:43.106 --> 01:03:45.106
Yes, thank you.

64
01:03:45.106 --> 01:03:49.106
Thank you for being so faithful.

65
01:03:49.106 --> 01:03:52.106
You are a big part of this house.

66
01:03:53.106 --> 01:03:56.106
You are a big part of this house.

67
01:03:56.106 --> 01:03:58.106
Just imagine if they weren't here.

68
01:04:08.106 --> 01:04:10.106
So let us bless them, let us encourage them.

69
01:04:10.106 --> 01:04:12.106
And I am so grateful for their faithfulness.

70
01:04:12.106 --> 01:04:14.106
I say that often and it is important.

71
01:04:17.106 --> 01:04:20.106
Sometimes we easily overlook those who are faithful.

72
01:04:23.106 --> 01:04:31.106
But let us be grateful and let us encourage those who serve every week.

73
01:04:34.106 --> 01:04:36.106
Lord, we thank You.

74
01:04:36.106 --> 01:04:38.106
And we love You.

75
01:04:43.106 --> 01:04:48.106
And we want to be aware of everything You have carried us through in 2024.

76
01:04:49.106 --> 01:04:51.106
There is no one like the Lord.

77
01:04:53.106 --> 01:04:54.106
So we bless Your name.

78
01:04:56.106 --> 01:04:57.106
The name of the Lord is worth.

79
01:05:00.106 --> 01:05:02.106
You are worthy to receive our praise.

80
01:05:07.106 --> 01:05:11.106
And I pray that we will be a house that will always praise Your name.

81
01:05:13.106 --> 01:05:14.106
In spirit and in truth.

82
01:05:15.106 --> 01:05:16.106
And I pray for Your people.

83
01:05:18.106 --> 01:05:19.106
That they will receive.

84
01:05:22.106 --> 01:05:23.106
Your Word.

85
01:05:25.106 --> 01:05:26.106
The Word that You have for us.

86
01:05:31.106 --> 01:05:33.106
Which will give us insight and wisdom for the days to come.

87
01:05:35.106 --> 01:05:36.106
Amen.

88
01:05:40.106 --> 01:05:41.106
If you have a Bible.

89
01:05:44.106 --> 01:05:45.106
Turn to John 1.

90
01:05:47.106 --> 01:05:48.106
Amen.

91
01:05:53.106 --> 01:05:57.106
I want to look at a number of things this morning.

92
01:05:58.106 --> 01:05:59.106
That I believe will give us insight.

93
01:06:00.106 --> 01:06:01.106
We thank God for what has been.

94
01:06:06.106 --> 01:06:08.106
But I want to give us caution for the year to come.

95
01:06:09.106 --> 01:06:11.106
And I also want to look ahead to the year to come.

96
01:06:18.106 --> 01:06:22.106
And I want to give three insights that I believe are significant for us.

97
01:06:23.106 --> 01:06:29.106
In the month of December, I always want to read the gospel of Luke and John.

98
01:06:31.106 --> 01:06:32.106
I want to be where the Lord has come.

99
01:06:34.106 --> 01:06:35.106
Where the story of Christ comes from.

100
01:06:44.106 --> 01:06:45.106
And this morning we will be in John 1.

101
01:06:47.106 --> 01:06:48.106
I am going to walk around a bit.

102
01:06:53.106 --> 01:06:54.106
But I have said this often.

103
01:06:56.106 --> 01:06:57.106
We are in a time of preparation.

104
01:06:59.106 --> 01:07:00.106
Amen.

105
01:07:02.106 --> 01:07:03.106
The whole earth is in preparation.

106
01:07:07.106 --> 01:07:08.106
For the King is coming back.

107
01:07:16.106 --> 01:07:20.106
So one of the ways we celebrate the Lord at Christmas is not just that baby in a manger.

108
01:07:22.106 --> 01:07:23.106
That is just the beginning.

109
01:07:29.106 --> 01:07:34.106
And without Him coming in the flesh, we would not have the cross and the sacrifice either.

110
01:07:38.106 --> 01:07:40.106
And we need that to enter the kingdom.

111
01:07:47.106 --> 01:07:51.106
Jesus says it. If you are not born again, you cannot enter the kingdom.

112
01:07:53.106 --> 01:07:58.106
You cannot enter the kingdom now without accepting the work of Christ.

113
01:08:06.106 --> 01:08:08.106
Church and kingdom, two different things. Amen.

114
01:08:11.106 --> 01:08:14.106
The church is a representation of what the kingdom is.

115
01:08:15.106 --> 01:08:16.106
It must be so.

116
01:08:16.106 --> 01:08:21.106
The church is a representation of what the kingdom is.

117
01:08:24.106 --> 01:08:28.106
For the church is the people who are born again.

118
01:08:34.106 --> 01:08:39.106
So we now live in the kingdom thanks to our regeneration.

119
01:08:39.106 --> 01:08:46.106
But we are reminded that He will come again.

120
01:08:50.106 --> 01:08:53.106
And that is the time frame we are in now.

121
01:08:55.106 --> 01:09:00.106
In history, the cross stands behind us, around us.

122
01:09:00.106 --> 01:09:09.106
For it is through the cross that we see the Lord. It is through the cross that we enter.

123
01:09:11.106 --> 01:09:13.106
It is through the cross that we live.

124
01:09:16.106 --> 01:09:19.106
He said, come to my cross and then take up your own.

125
01:09:23.106 --> 01:09:26.106
So this life is a life of dying to live.

126
01:09:27.106 --> 01:09:28.106
And that is the kingdom.

127
01:09:31.106 --> 01:09:33.106
Until you die, you do not live for Christ.

128
01:09:35.106 --> 01:09:36.106
For it is an offering.

129
01:09:51.106 --> 01:09:56.106
It is important to give out of obedience as a sacrifice.

130
01:09:56.106 --> 01:09:58.106
And then that joy will come afterwards.

131
01:10:01.106 --> 01:10:06.106
For if you wait for a feeling, you will not get there.

132
01:10:07.106 --> 01:10:08.106
And that applies to everything.

133
01:10:09.106 --> 01:10:10.106
That applies to your worship.

134
01:10:13.106 --> 01:10:17.106
That applies to your life thrown away, how you see the Lord.

135
01:10:21.106 --> 01:10:25.106
If you wait until your soul tells you it is time, you will never enter.

136
01:10:31.106 --> 01:10:34.106
Jesus does not say, feel it and then do it.

137
01:10:35.106 --> 01:10:40.106
Jesus says, do it and see how my spirit fills your soul.

138
01:10:42.106 --> 01:10:43.106
And that is the kingdom.

139
01:10:46.106 --> 01:10:48.106
And the kingdom is through the spirit.

140
01:10:49.106 --> 01:10:51.106
Okay, so we look to him.

141
01:10:51.106 --> 01:10:52.106
He has come.

142
01:10:52.106 --> 01:10:53.106
We are divided.

143
01:10:53.106 --> 01:10:54.106
We are renewed.

144
01:10:54.106 --> 01:10:55.106
We live by the Spirit.

145
01:10:55.106 --> 01:10:56.106
And He is coming again.

146
01:11:03.106 --> 01:11:04.106
And this is the preparation.

147
01:11:06.106 --> 01:11:07.106
We are being prepared.

148
01:11:09.106 --> 01:11:11.106
We are being prepared to meet the Lord.

149
01:11:13.106 --> 01:11:15.106
And I want to take a look at John the Baptist.

150
01:11:19.106 --> 01:11:22.106
For John the Baptist was the forerunner of Jesus.

151
01:11:26.106 --> 01:11:31.106
John the Baptist is naturally about three months older than Jesus.

152
01:11:35.106 --> 01:11:39.106
And we know that I am not going to read the whole story, but John is prophesied.

153
01:11:40.106 --> 01:11:47.106
He was told that his life would be a forerunning ministry to prepare the way for Jesus Christ.

154
01:11:48.106 --> 01:11:55.106
And we know that the ministry of John is a forerunning ministry that paves the way for Jesus Christ.

155
01:11:59.106 --> 01:12:00.106
He was a prophet.

156
01:12:01.106 --> 01:12:09.106
When the conception took place, the Lord already spoke to Zacharias, his father, that he would be a prophet for all Israel.

157
01:12:22.106 --> 01:12:27.106
And John would prepare a way for the first coming of the Lord.

158
01:12:31.106 --> 01:12:33.106
And this is how the Lord works.

159
01:12:41.106 --> 01:12:45.106
The Lord always sends people ahead to prepare a people for Himself.

160
01:12:47.106 --> 01:12:48.106
He gives time.

161
01:12:49.106 --> 01:12:50.106
He gives people.

162
01:12:51.106 --> 01:12:53.106
To prophesy the Word of the Lord.

163
01:12:53.106 --> 01:12:58.106
To bring that message so that the people will be ready to receive him when he comes.

164
01:13:10.106 --> 01:13:16.106
So John had a forerunner ministry for the ministry of Jesus.

165
01:13:24.106 --> 01:13:26.106
And the Bible shows us patterns.

166
01:13:38.106 --> 01:13:46.106
God will also send messengers ahead for his second coming to prepare for the coming of the King.

167
01:13:47.106 --> 01:13:55.106
And John did not just bring a message.

168
01:13:57.106 --> 01:13:58.106
He lived a message.

169
01:14:03.106 --> 01:14:06.106
If you know about John, he lived in the wilderness.

170
01:14:08.106 --> 01:14:09.106
He is set apart.

171
01:14:11.106 --> 01:14:12.106
He wore strange clothes.

172
01:14:12.106 --> 01:14:14.106
He eats locusts and honey.

173
01:14:17.106 --> 01:14:21.106
What it tells you is that he was not part of the culture.

174
01:14:24.106 --> 01:14:25.106
He was not there for that.

175
01:14:27.106 --> 01:14:29.106
His life was set apart by the Lord.

176
01:14:32.106 --> 01:14:34.106
So that he could speak into the culture of that day.

177
01:14:37.106 --> 01:14:39.106
That is the nature of prophetic ministry.

178
01:14:43.106 --> 01:14:45.106
They do not live with the majority.

179
01:14:51.106 --> 01:14:53.106
They do not get their input from that majority.

180
01:14:55.106 --> 01:14:56.106
They hear from God.

181
01:14:59.106 --> 01:15:01.106
And they speak in the culture of the day.

182
01:15:06.106 --> 01:15:09.106
For prophetic ministry is different from pastoral ministry.

183
01:15:13.106 --> 01:15:15.106
There are different ministries for the people.

184
01:15:20.106 --> 01:15:24.106
And John was called to live set apart, blown upon.

185
01:15:29.106 --> 01:15:31.106
For when you prepare a way for the Lord,

186
01:15:34.106 --> 01:15:36.106
you must also bring correction into it.

187
01:15:39.106 --> 01:15:40.106
You must bring reformation.

188
01:15:43.106 --> 01:15:44.106
It is not a popular ministry.

189
01:15:50.106 --> 01:15:53.106
For it will push, it will pull, and it will try to get to your flesh.

190
01:16:08.106 --> 01:16:09.106
It is not an easy ministry.

191
01:16:10.106 --> 01:16:13.106
For the Lord says, it is important that the people get moving,

192
01:16:13.106 --> 01:16:15.106
so that they are ready when I come.

193
01:16:18.106 --> 01:16:20.106
It is a different message than a pastoral message.

194
01:16:32.106 --> 01:16:35.106
And John the Baptist received the assignment,

195
01:16:36.106 --> 01:16:38.106
you cannot be part of that crowd.

196
01:16:39.106 --> 01:16:40.106
You are set apart.

197
01:16:41.106 --> 01:16:43.106
Do not live like him, do not look like him.

198
01:16:44.106 --> 01:16:46.106
For you will receive that message from heaven.

199
01:16:50.106 --> 01:16:53.106
Let us read John 1, verse 19 and see what he says.

200
01:17:06.106 --> 01:17:08.106
This is the testimony of John the Baptist.

201
01:17:09.106 --> 01:17:12.106
The Jews had sent priests and Levites from Jerusalem to ask him

202
01:17:12.106 --> 01:17:14.106
who are you?

203
01:17:19.106 --> 01:17:22.106
And he answered without hesitation and declared openly,

204
01:17:23.106 --> 01:17:24.106
I am not the Messiah.

205
01:17:27.106 --> 01:17:29.106
And then they asked him, who are you? Are you Elijah?

206
01:17:30.106 --> 01:17:32.106
And that was a correct question.

207
01:17:35.106 --> 01:17:36.106
And he said, I am not he.

208
01:17:41.106 --> 01:17:46.106
And yet Jesus later says that John acted in the spirit of Elijah.

209
01:17:51.106 --> 01:17:54.106
And then they asked him, who are you? Are you Elijah?

210
01:17:54.106 --> 01:17:55.106
And he said, I am not he.

211
01:17:58.106 --> 01:18:01.106
And yet Jesus later says that John acted in the spirit of Elijah.

212
01:18:05.106 --> 01:18:07.106
Elijah was indeed the prophet of that time.

213
01:18:11.106 --> 01:18:13.106
And according to the Scriptures, he would come again.

214
01:18:24.106 --> 01:18:26.106
And if he receives him, then he is the one who prepares the way.

215
01:18:30.106 --> 01:18:31.106
So they ask, are you then the prophet?

216
01:18:35.106 --> 01:18:38.106
And then they finally asked him, but who are you then?

217
01:18:55.106 --> 01:19:02.106
And John answered, I am the voice that cries in the wilderness, make straight the way of the Lord, as the prophet Jesus has said.

218
01:19:05.106 --> 01:19:07.106
John understood who he was.

219
01:19:08.106 --> 01:19:14.106
He knew that he was there to show the people of Israel in preparation.

220
01:19:30.106 --> 01:19:32.106
To go through the water of baptism.

221
01:19:35.106 --> 01:19:36.106
To be able to receive the Messiah.

222
01:19:38.106 --> 01:19:39.106
So that they would see him.

223
01:19:44.106 --> 01:19:46.106
They had to be able to recognize Jesus.

224
01:20:02.106 --> 01:20:05.106
And we see here that Jesus is on his way.

225
01:20:06.106 --> 01:20:09.106
John faithfully delivers his message to Israel.

226
01:20:12.106 --> 01:20:13.106
He is faithful in the wilderness.

227
01:20:16.106 --> 01:20:18.106
He is faithful in preaching the Word.

228
01:20:24.106 --> 01:20:28.106
And you see then in verse 29 that one day Jesus comes to him.

229
01:20:31.106 --> 01:20:32.106
And this is what John then says.

230
01:20:35.106 --> 01:20:37.106
The next day John saw Jesus coming toward him.

231
01:20:47.106 --> 01:20:49.106
And he said, there is the Lamb of God.

232
01:20:53.106 --> 01:20:54.106
Who takes away the sin of the world.

233
01:21:00.106 --> 01:21:02.106
This is his reaction as Jesus comes to him.

234
01:21:06.106 --> 01:21:08.106
The word see or look or behold.

235
01:21:09.106 --> 01:21:11.106
The word look or behold is the key.

236
01:21:20.106 --> 01:21:22.106
For this was the ministry of John.

237
01:21:23.106 --> 01:21:24.106
What was he doing?

238
01:21:25.106 --> 01:21:28.106
He was preparing the people to rightly see Jesus.

239
01:21:36.106 --> 01:21:40.106
So that they could receive him and give their lives to him at the moment he came.

240
01:21:49.106 --> 01:21:52.106
And back in September, I gave a number of keys for 2025.

241
01:21:58.106 --> 01:22:01.106
And one of the meanings of the coming year is salvation.

242
01:22:06.106 --> 01:22:08.106
The coming year is truly being able to see that.

243
01:22:13.106 --> 01:22:16.106
And does that also mean being disturbed?

244
01:22:25.106 --> 01:22:26.106
A disruption.

245
01:22:36.106 --> 01:22:38.106
And those two go hand in hand.

246
01:22:47.106 --> 01:22:52.106
For at the moment that John says, look, this is the one for whom I have prepared the way.

247
01:23:00.106 --> 01:23:02.106
The impact of that must change lives.

248
01:23:06.106 --> 01:23:09.106
It halts their lives. It interrupts everything that is going on.

249
01:23:14.106 --> 01:23:16.106
It interrupts that normal pattern of life.

250
01:23:20.106 --> 01:23:23.106
If you truly see the Lamb that was slain.

251
01:23:27.106 --> 01:23:29.106
